{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Who has not been freed.</b> That is, the sin is lighter here because the betrothal of the designated wife was not formally acquired, and the essence of the sin is only that he profaned the holy thing of HaShem by lying with a half-slave woman. And since this act is contrary to the dignity of the man who acts, not to the dignity of the woman acted upon, there is no doubt that she habituated him and is fit to be flogged. Now, one who commits this intentionally — having done this folly to profane himself — is close to inadvertent, and brings a guilt-offering for the profanation of the holy thing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:57.350199562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}